.TH buffer_prefetch 3
.SH NAME
buffer_prefetch \- ensure a minimum number of bytes are available in the buffer
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <buffer.h>

ssize_t \fBbuffer_prefetch\fP(buffer* \fIb\fP, size_t \fIn\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbuffer_prefetch\fP ensures that at least \fIn\fP bytes are available in the 
buffer \fIb\fP, starting from the current read position (\fIb->p\fP).

If the requested number of bytes (\fIn\fP) is already present in the buffer 
(i.e., \fIb->n - b->p >= n\fP), the function returns the number of bytes 
currently available.

If the buffer does not contain enough data, \fBbuffer_prefetch\fP attempts 
to refill the buffer using the underlying read operation (\fIb->op\fP). 
If the current read position is not at the beginning of the buffer, the 
existing data is moved to the start of the buffer first to maximize available 
space. It continues reading until at least \fIn\fP bytes are available, 
an error occurs, or end-of-file is reached.

For memory-mapped buffers, if the requested amount is not available because 
the file is shorter than requested, the function returns the remaining data 
in the current window.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the total number of bytes available in the buffer starting from 
the current pointer \fIb->p\fP, or -1 on error.

.SH SEE ALSO
buffer_init(3), buffer_feed(3), buffer_freshen(3)